{
 "gdd": "horror-entities",
 "blocking": [
  "HE-19, HE-11, HE-12, HE-14(f), HE-20, HE-25; Dependencies (Layout row, L927); Open Question 32 (L1769); AC-HE-14, 16, 41, 51, 52, 127, 128, 141, 142: [main review; creative-director spot-check confirmed] This is the second review's blocker 2, and it is still open. HE-19 builds `linked`, `connected`, the passable-leaf test, the standoff, ingress legality and all pathing on `door_passage(section_id, via_id)`. Layout does not publish that read: grep finds `door_passage` only in horror-entities.md, and the Horror GDD's own Dependencies row (L927) says it is 'required and not yet published'. Layout routes door openness through the Graph's published `opening(edge_id) -> {area, area_max, door_state}` (LY L657, L1341). The Horror GDD never cites that read. So the CALM standoff and step-away invariant, which is the non-lethal-presence promise behind the 'told, fair, unarmed' pillar, rests on a contract nobody owns. Every lethal-loop AC that depends on it reads NOT ASSESSED or can only run against a stub.",
  "AC-HE-88 vs AC-HE-130 and HE-F5; E-HE-18; Player Fantasy worked moment: [main review rated RECOMMENDED; creative-director raises to BLOCKING] Both rows are BLOCKING acceptance criteria, and they pin opposite outcomes for the same fixture. AC-HE-130 uses the exact HE-F5 convention, under which a walker 5 ticks late (a=59) is clear at U=95 on a cardinal octant. AC-HE-88 uses a +1 convention and says that walker is hit on the draw of 95. I confirmed the AC-HE-88 text is present. No build can pass both rows, so the gate cannot go green. The rows also disagree about the strike-fairness margin, which is the moment the horror pillar depends on ('just made it', never 'hit where I was not'). Even a small fix here needs to land before implementation."
 ],
 "disagreements": [
  "[creative-director vs main review] Severity of the AC-HE-88 / AC-HE-130 conflict. The main review rated it RECOMMENDED. I rate it BLOCKING because both are BLOCKING ACs that no single build can satisfy, so the gate cannot pass. The conflict also sits on the strike-fairness margin, which is the core of the 'readable, fair, unarmed' horror pillar. It is still a targeted edit, so the verdict stays NEEDS REVISION, not MAJOR.",
  "[creative-director, partial agreement] On the door_passage blocker I recommend option (a), conforming to the Graph's published opening() plus Layout's rects_in. The main review left both options open. Option (b) adds a new cross-GDD contract on the system that has already said it does not own door state (LY-35). That makes a third carry-over likely."
 ]
